            <h2>What is a Mock API?</h2>
            <p>
                A mock API is a simulated backend that behaves like a real REST API. 
                Instead of connecting to a real database, developers send requests to a fake API that returns predefined JSON responses.
            </p>
            <p>
                This allows frontend developers to build UI, test requests, and simulate real API interactions before the backend exists.
            </p>

